Problem Statement : 
Write a solution to find the students who meet the following criteria:

1. Have taken all mandatory courses and at least two elective courses offered in their major.
2. Achieved a grade of A in all mandatory courses and at least B in elective courses.
3. Maintained an average GPA of at least 2.5 across all their courses (including those outside their major).

Return the result table ordered by student_id in ascending order.



MS SQL Server management studio solution:


/*Maintained an average GPA of at least 2.5 across all their courses (including those outside their major)*/
with valid_student  as (select avg(gpa) average_gpa ,student_id  from [enrollments] group by student_id having  avg(gpa)>2.5),


/*the valid students taken courses and really enrolled*/
  student_status  as (
select t1.student_id,t3.mandatory,t4.grade from valid_student t1
						inner join [dbo].[students] t2 on t1.student_id=t2.student_id
						inner join [dbo].[courses] t3 on t2.major=t3.major
						left join [dbo].[enrollments]  t4 on t1.student_id=t4.student_id and t3.course_id=t4.course_id
						)

, 
aggegated_report as (
select student_id , sum(case when mandatory='true' then 1 else 0 end) as total_mandatory_course,
					sum(case when (mandatory='true' and grade='A') then 1 else 0 end) as total_gradeA_mandatory_course,
					sum(case when mandatory='false' and grade is not null then 1 else 0 end) as total_taken_elective_course,
					sum(case when mandatory ='false' and grade in ('A', 'B') then 1 else 0 end)  as total_elective_good_grades
					from student_status 
					group by student_id
					)

					select student_id from aggegated_report
					where total_mandatory_course=total_gradeA_mandatory_course
					and total_taken_elective_course>=2
					and total_taken_elective_course=total_elective_good_grades

